  "conclusion": [
    "Named first-use lookup contributes substantial latency in this no-op comparison. It cannot explain every slow access to an already warmed owner host.",
    "Random IDs reduced the median first-use wait but produced an 11074ms outlier. They would require a durable authoritative wallet/material locator before use for real signing.",
    "APAC hints did not consistently help across the two captured invocations. This test does not support a hardcoded placement change.",
    "Retain deterministic owner host routing and the existing registration prewarm. No new full-signing speedup was measured."
  ],
